1
00:01:25,686 --> 00:01:29,714
Five dollars and 29 cents?

2
00:01:29,890 --> 00:01:32,485
They've got to be kidding.

3
00:01:32,659 --> 00:01:34,150
Uh... Ahem.

4
00:01:34,628 --> 00:01:38,156
Uh... Excuse me.
Excuse me. Excuse me.

5
00:01:38,332 --> 00:01:41,496
Surely you've got something smaller.
- Sorry.

6
00:01:41,668 --> 00:01:44,729
I bet they charge half this much
down at the Pharmacy Mart.

7
00:01:44,905 --> 00:01:46,737
Oh, I know they do. I
shop there all the time.

8
00:01:46,907 --> 00:01:48,933
Well, how come you
charge so much here?

9
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:51,203
Sir, you're not
buying just bandages.

10
00:01:51,378 --> 00:01:53,506
You're buying
convenience, free parking,

11
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,342
our charm and good looks.

12
00:01:55,515 --> 00:01:56,949
Don't move.

13
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:59,609
Hands up, both of you.
Lie down on the floor. Now!

14
00:02:02,723 --> 00:02:04,954
Open that thing. Hurry up!

15
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:07,390
Lie down. Do it!

16
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:15,000
All right. Just stay
put, both of you.

17
00:02:15,168 --> 00:02:17,501
Don't even think about moving
till I'm long gone. You hear?

18
00:02:17,671 --> 00:02:20,140
I'm watching you.
You just stay put.

19
00:02:25,746 --> 00:02:26,805
<i>Y4J7.</i>

20
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:42,525
Lucky guess, that's all it was.
Lucky for you, unlucky for my client.

21
00:02:42,696 --> 00:02:44,392
Aw, come on, Dave.
Be a good sport.

22
00:02:44,564 --> 00:02:45,924
The robber was
wearing a ski mask.

23
00:02:46,066 --> 00:02:47,864
That lineup was a
joke and you know it.

24
00:02:48,035 --> 00:02:51,233
Maybe I didn't see his face, but I
got a good look at everything else.

25
00:02:51,405 --> 00:02:53,704
- His shoes and everything.
- And his car.

26
00:02:53,874 --> 00:02:56,354
Somebody stole my client's car
and used it to commit the crime.

27
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:58,706
- Happens every day.
- Save it for the jury, Dave.

28
00:02:58,879 --> 00:03:01,314
You think because you're Ben
Matlock, the jury's gonna lap up

29
00:03:01,481 --> 00:03:02,841
whatever you put
in front of them.

30
00:03:02,983 --> 00:03:04,423
- Lap that up, Dave.
- Hey, Ben. Ben.

31
00:03:04,584 --> 00:03:08,180
Oh, go ahead. Touch me
and I'll get you for assault.

32
00:03:08,388 --> 00:03:10,118
Jerk.

33
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:14,051
Takes one to know one.

34
00:03:17,531 --> 00:03:18,999
Let's see now.

35
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,260
You'd like us to issue
a stop-work order

36
00:03:21,435 --> 00:03:24,269
on a Jacuzzi that's being
built in Mr. Ramsey's backyard?

37
00:03:24,438 --> 00:03:26,270
That's right. He's my
next-door neighbor,

38
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:30,241
and he's building that thing
less than 15 feet from my house.

39
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:33,073
The noise of the motor
by itself would be awful,

40
00:03:33,246 --> 00:03:36,614
to say nothing of all
those half-naked people

41
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:39,082
that'll be jumping in
and out of it and yelling.

42
00:03:39,519 --> 00:03:43,149
He's just mad because it's so close
to his fence, he won't be able to peep.

43
00:03:43,323 --> 00:03:46,521
Peep? I'll have you know,
sir, I'm a church-going person.

44
00:03:46,693 --> 00:03:47,956
You gray-haired old man.

45
00:03:48,128 --> 00:03:49,619
- I'll gray-hair you.
- Gentlemen.

46
00:03:49,796 --> 00:03:52,316
None of my other neighbors are
complaining about what I'm doing.

47
00:03:52,466 --> 00:03:53,490
The neighbors moved away.

48
00:03:53,667 --> 00:03:55,659
- Mr. Matlock, please.
- Sir.

49
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:59,332
He's in violation of the
property-line setback

50
00:03:59,506 --> 00:04:03,102
clearly delineated in
the deed to his property.

51
00:04:03,276 --> 00:04:05,472
Here's the...
See, I have a right.

52
00:04:05,645 --> 00:04:09,946
It states that no one in
our neighborhood may build

53
00:04:10,117 --> 00:04:12,814
within 5 feet of his or her
property lines without a variance,

54
00:04:12,986 --> 00:04:15,615
and I'm not about
to give it to him.

55
00:04:16,456 --> 00:04:20,223
Uh, Mr. Matlock, this isn't
the deed to his property.

56
00:04:20,393 --> 00:04:23,522
It's the deed to Jimmy
Carter's home in Plains.

57
00:04:27,901 --> 00:04:28,941
Did you put that in there?

58
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:30,662
How was I supposed
to put that in there?

59
00:04:30,804 --> 00:04:32,966
How dare you?

60
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:35,575
Oh. Uh, um... Heh.

61
00:04:35,742 --> 00:04:38,439
I'm Cliff Lewis. I'm
Mr. Matlock's associate.

62
00:04:38,612 --> 00:04:41,875
Oh, yeah. Um... Uh... Heh.

63
00:04:42,048 --> 00:04:44,711
We're obviously having a
little bit of a problem here.

64
00:04:44,885 --> 00:04:50,017
Um, how about if I faxed you a copy of
that deed by the end of the afternoon?

65
00:04:52,559 --> 00:04:54,027
Very well.

66
00:04:54,194 --> 00:04:57,995
This case will be continued
till 9 a.m. tomorrow.

67
00:04:58,165 --> 00:04:59,326
Next case.

68
00:04:59,499 --> 00:05:02,435
You're nuttier than a
fruitcake. You know that?

69
00:05:02,602 --> 00:05:05,436
- Are you sure you had the deed?
- Yeah, I put it in here this morning.

70
00:05:05,605 --> 00:05:08,939
I don't walk around with the deed to
Jimmy Carter's house in my briefcase.

71
00:05:09,109 --> 00:05:13,638
All right, I'll take care of the fax.
You go home and take a shower.

72
00:05:13,814 --> 00:05:14,838
No.

73
00:05:15,015 --> 00:05:17,776
Didn't you tell me you had a surprise
party for Judge Cooksey tonight?

74
00:05:17,918 --> 00:05:19,784
Oh, that's right. And
you'll send the fax?

75
00:05:19,953 --> 00:05:22,946
Yeah, I'll take care...
Yeah, I'll take care of it.

76
00:05:36,069 --> 00:05:38,595
Well, Mr. Matlock,
good to see you again.

77
00:05:38,772 --> 00:05:39,796
Nice to see you.

78
00:05:39,973 --> 00:05:41,771
My, aren't we all
decked out this evening.

79
00:05:41,942 --> 00:05:44,502
- What's the occasion?
- Judge Cooksey's party.

80
00:05:45,679 --> 00:05:47,477
- Whose party? MATLOCK:
Richard Cooksey.

81
00:05:47,914 --> 00:05:51,749
Surprise birthday party.
Invitation said, uh, black tie.

82
00:05:51,918 --> 00:05:54,251
MAîTRE D': Uh, you're
sure the party's here?

83
00:05:54,421 --> 00:05:55,480
Sure.

84
00:05:55,655 --> 00:05:59,148
In the Fountain
Room, 7:30 tonight.

85
00:05:59,326 --> 00:06:02,558
I'm afraid there's been some
kind of misunderstanding.

86
00:06:03,296 --> 00:06:05,492
I RSVP'd and everything.

87
00:06:05,665 --> 00:06:07,625
MAîTRE D': Yes, but
there's no party here tonight.

88
00:06:07,767 --> 00:06:08,791
I left a message.

89
00:06:09,269 --> 00:06:11,795
Well, perhaps you should
check your invitation.

90
00:06:11,972 --> 00:06:13,463
I didn't make a mistake.

91
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:18,101
Mr. Matlock, the Bourne wedding
party is in the Fountain Room tonight.

92
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:24,017
Well, where's Judge
Cooksey's party?

93
00:06:24,184 --> 00:06:26,176
Not here.

94
00:06:28,555 --> 00:06:30,387
Right there.

95
00:06:30,690 --> 00:06:33,524
See? Somebody's trying to
make me look like a jackass.

96
00:06:34,127 --> 00:06:35,618
- It's him.
- Who's him?

97
00:06:35,795 --> 00:06:36,990
Dave Burton.

98
00:06:37,163 --> 00:06:40,531
That lawyer that's representing that
guy that robbed that convenience store.

99
00:06:40,934 --> 00:06:44,996
He's trying to make me look nuts
so he can discredit me as a witness.

100
00:06:45,171 --> 00:06:48,266
First at the hearing
and then at this party.

101
00:06:49,209 --> 00:06:52,611
Ben, this invitation was mailed
two days before the robbery.

102
00:06:52,979 --> 00:06:54,811
- No.
- Yeah, look at the postmark.

103
00:06:54,981 --> 00:06:56,581
And how could he have
switched the deeds?

104
00:07:01,154 --> 00:07:02,178
Hello?

105
00:07:02,355 --> 00:07:04,675
WOMAN: <i>You have a nice day?</i>

106
00:07:04,824 --> 00:07:06,224
<i>- I know I did.</i>
- Who's this?

107
00:07:06,393 --> 00:07:09,727
<i>That's for me to know
and you to never find out.</i>

108
00:07:09,896 --> 00:07:12,832
<i>If you thought today was
fun, just wait till tomorrow.</i>

109
00:07:12,999 --> 00:07:14,023
Who is this?

110
00:07:20,006 --> 00:07:21,030
Who was that?

111
00:07:21,841 --> 00:07:23,605
It wasn't Dave Burton.

112
00:07:35,388 --> 00:07:37,516
Who else got one of these?

113
00:07:37,691 --> 00:07:39,956
I don't know. I
didn't ask anybody.

114
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:42,152
- It was supposed to be a secret.
- Good morning.

115
00:07:42,329 --> 00:07:43,558
- Good morning.
- Hey, Cliff.

116
00:07:43,730 --> 00:07:45,730
Hey, Conrad, did Ben
tell you what happened?

117
00:07:45,899 --> 00:07:48,664
Yeah. Somebody should check out
this phone number, don't you think?

118
00:07:48,835 --> 00:07:50,133
Well, I did.

119
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:54,240
It's a voice-mail number for,
uh, some insurance company.

120
00:07:54,407 --> 00:07:57,275
- What'd they say?
- They said, "That explains it."

121
00:07:57,444 --> 00:08:00,039
- Explains what?
- The message they got two weeks ago

122
00:08:00,213 --> 00:08:03,115
from some guy who said
that he'd be at the party

123
00:08:03,283 --> 00:08:05,123
but wasn't thrilled about
having to rent a tux.

124
00:08:05,285 --> 00:08:07,083
They just figured that
it was a wrong number.

125
00:08:07,253 --> 00:08:08,813
I was the only one that called?

126
00:08:08,955 --> 00:08:11,288
My feeling is, you were the
only one who got an invitation.

127
00:08:11,458 --> 00:08:12,721
Somebody means business.

128
00:08:12,892 --> 00:08:14,212
Well, we know it's a woman.

129
00:08:14,361 --> 00:08:16,023
Mm. Probably Dave Burton.

130
00:08:16,196 --> 00:08:20,031
He got his secretary
or some friend to call.

131
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,135
Or maybe it's somebody
with an ax to grind,

132
00:08:22,302 --> 00:08:23,542
maybe on the back of your neck.

133
00:08:23,703 --> 00:08:26,832
- That's no way to talk.
- Hey, I'm sorry.

134
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:30,435
Ax to grind on the
back of my neck.

135
00:08:30,877 --> 00:08:33,346
Who? CONRAD: Joanna Wilton.

136
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:35,313
Early last month, she
was paroled from prison.

137
00:08:35,448 --> 00:08:36,472
Who's Joanna Wilton?

138
00:08:36,649 --> 00:08:39,619
She was George Wilton's
wife. He was a contractor.

139
00:08:39,786 --> 00:08:43,621
She was having an affair with her
personal trainer, Harry Slade. Heh.

140
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:45,350
- Oh, he was something, huh? Heh.
- Heh.

141
00:08:45,492 --> 00:08:47,586
- What do you mean? What?
- Ha, ha.

142
00:08:47,761 --> 00:08:51,425
At the same time he was having
an affair with Joanna Wilton,

143
00:08:51,598 --> 00:08:55,057
he was having an affair
with George Wilton's mistress.

144
00:08:55,235 --> 00:08:58,035
Yeah, but remember, it was the other
woman he was having an affair with

145
00:08:58,204 --> 00:08:59,604
that caused all the problems.

146
00:08:59,773 --> 00:09:01,901
Oh, Harry, you've wrecked me.

147
00:09:02,075 --> 00:09:04,840
<i>The first woman was
George Wilton's wife, Joanna.</i>

148
00:09:05,011 --> 00:09:09,472
Sorry I didn't get a chance
to, you know, work you out.

149
00:09:09,649 --> 00:09:11,311
Mm, that's all right.

150
00:09:11,985 --> 00:09:14,477
I feel very tuned up.

151
00:09:16,256 --> 00:09:17,280
Mwah.

152
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:20,792
- Where are you going?
- Oh, baby, it's late.

153
00:09:23,696 --> 00:09:26,530
- Here.
- Oh. What is this?

154
00:09:26,699 --> 00:09:28,827
Go ahead, open it.

155
00:09:32,338 --> 00:09:34,637
<i>Tropic of Capricorn,</i>
Henry Miller. Whoa.

156
00:09:36,309 --> 00:09:37,470
Read the inscription.

157
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:41,006
Oh. Joanna.

158
00:09:42,282 --> 00:09:43,944
How can I thank you?

159
00:09:55,962 --> 00:09:57,562
<i>The second woman
Harry was seeing</i>

160
00:09:57,730 --> 00:09:59,756
<i>was George Wilton's
mistress, Bridget.</i>

161
00:10:01,167 --> 00:10:03,227
Harry. What are you doing here?

162
00:10:03,403 --> 00:10:06,202
Oh. Bridget, I need to talk.

163
00:10:06,372 --> 00:10:08,534
Talk? You?

164
00:10:10,176 --> 00:10:12,338
Bridget, please?

165
00:10:13,713 --> 00:10:15,875
Okay, come on.

166
00:10:31,898 --> 00:10:37,303
"Harry, you're the
best. Love, Joanna."

167
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:40,064
What the hell?

168
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:42,209
Joanna, what is this?

169
00:10:42,375 --> 00:10:44,571
- What?
- Who's Harry?

170
00:10:44,744 --> 00:10:45,803
Your personal trainer.

171
00:10:45,979 --> 00:10:48,312
- George, your blood pressure...
- In our bed?!

172
00:11:04,998 --> 00:11:06,638
<i>George went over
to confront Harry</i>

173
00:11:06,766 --> 00:11:09,235
<i>and found one big surprise.</i>

174
00:11:22,282 --> 00:11:24,114
Men didn't come this morning.

175
00:11:24,284 --> 00:11:27,413
- Well, they forgot.
- Forgot?

176
00:11:28,087 --> 00:11:30,215
Look, I'm building a
shopping center in Somerville.

177
00:11:30,390 --> 00:11:33,417
Soon as I can spare a couple of
guys, I'll send them to your house.

178
00:11:33,593 --> 00:11:35,619
My easy chair got
soaked last night.

179
00:11:35,795 --> 00:11:39,027
I've been sitting in it for
years. It fits my body like skin.

180
00:11:39,199 --> 00:11:41,566
It's irreplaceable. What
are you gonna do about it?

181
00:11:41,734 --> 00:11:44,966
I didn't call you down here to talk
about your roof or your easy chair.

182
00:11:45,138 --> 00:11:48,108
I called you down here because I'm
being charged with first-degree murder.

183
00:11:48,274 --> 00:11:50,937
And I want you to defend me.
I'm willing to pay you twice your fee.

184
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:00,418
Yes?

185
00:12:02,088 --> 00:12:03,613
What the hell are
you doing here?

186
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:07,818
George? I'm here trying to find
out about the women in Harry's life.

187
00:12:07,994 --> 00:12:09,519
What the hell are
you doing here?

188
00:12:09,696 --> 00:12:12,256
You're supposed to be
climbing my roof, not her.

189
00:12:12,999 --> 00:12:14,058
Well, I was...

190
00:12:14,434 --> 00:12:16,926
Did you say "the
women in Harry's life"?

191
00:12:20,173 --> 00:12:21,197
Bridget.

192
00:12:21,774 --> 00:12:24,835
George, listen to me.
Harry was a long time ago.

193
00:12:25,011 --> 00:12:26,536
Pack up your stuff
and get out of here.

194
00:12:26,713 --> 00:12:28,443
- George... GEORGE:
And leave the jewelry.

195
00:12:28,615 --> 00:12:30,215
- Hold it. GEORGE:
You heard me. Get out.

196
00:12:30,383 --> 00:12:31,976
- Hold it!
- What?!

197
00:12:32,151 --> 00:12:35,815
She's not going
anywhere, you are.

198
00:12:35,989 --> 00:12:37,958
And not a word
of this to anybody.

199
00:12:38,558 --> 00:12:41,653
- I own this house. She's out.
- Are you out of your mind?

200
00:12:41,828 --> 00:12:45,595
If one word gets out about Harry
having an affair with your wife

201
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:49,759
and your mistress,
the DA will kill us, fast.

202
00:12:51,304 --> 00:12:54,866
Mom, uh, this is Miss Thomas.
She's one of George's attorneys.

203
00:12:55,041 --> 00:12:57,033
I have a few questions,
if you don't mind.

204
00:12:57,210 --> 00:12:59,076
<i>Ten and...</i>

205
00:13:00,847 --> 00:13:01,871
Bobbie.

206
00:13:02,548 --> 00:13:03,572
I wanna hear this.

207
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:09,979
Bobbie.

208
00:13:11,891 --> 00:13:13,587
Bobbie's from my first marriage.

209
00:13:14,594 --> 00:13:17,325
When you have kids young,
you can't lie about your age.

210
00:13:17,497 --> 00:13:19,056
It drives me crazy.

211
00:13:19,232 --> 00:13:20,632
I imagine.

212
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:24,032
You told the police Harry
got to the house at 10:15.

213
00:13:24,203 --> 00:13:26,365
The guesthouse, yeah.

214
00:13:26,539 --> 00:13:28,599
Oh. Um...

215
00:13:30,710 --> 00:13:32,542
Why the guesthouse?

216
00:13:32,712 --> 00:13:35,773
Miss Thomas? Where
else would I entertain Harry?

217
00:13:38,284 --> 00:13:41,618
Um, Harry left his
house around 9.

218
00:13:41,788 --> 00:13:43,757
Did he say what
took him so long?

219
00:13:44,290 --> 00:13:45,918
No.

220
00:13:46,092 --> 00:13:48,152
And I didn't waste time asking.

221
00:13:49,095 --> 00:13:52,532
I suppose you have an alibi
for the time of the murder.

222
00:13:52,699 --> 00:13:55,567
No. I don't need one.

223
00:13:55,735 --> 00:13:58,500
I didn't kill Harry.

224
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:00,196
This is kind of hard.

225
00:14:00,373 --> 00:14:03,138
I mean, uh, this is a secret.

226
00:14:03,309 --> 00:14:06,302
Secrets have a way of
coming out in a murder trial.

227
00:14:06,479 --> 00:14:09,643
Well, that's what
I'm afraid of. Uh...

228
00:14:11,617 --> 00:14:15,281
It's about where Harry was for
an hour before he saw my mom.

229
00:14:16,055 --> 00:14:17,079
Yeah?

230
00:14:18,891 --> 00:14:20,189
He was with me.

231
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,294
He was with you?

232
00:14:24,330 --> 00:14:28,267
Boy, this guy must
have been truly amazing.

233
00:14:28,935 --> 00:14:30,665
<i>Ben finally pieced
the case together</i>

234
00:14:30,837 --> 00:14:34,274
<i>two days after falling off a ladder
trying to fix the roof of his house.</i>

235
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:37,433
The night before the murder, uh,

236
00:14:37,610 --> 00:14:42,776
you, I guess you could
say, oh, uh, rendezvoused

237
00:14:42,949 --> 00:14:45,509
with Harry out there in
the guesthouse, didn't you?

238
00:14:45,685 --> 00:14:46,709
That's true.

239
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:48,946
And you'd been doing
that in the guesthouse

240
