479
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:23,563
was because of these drawings
done by Jimmy Johnson.

480
00:28:23,735 --> 00:28:26,227
See? Now, here's...

481
00:28:26,672 --> 00:28:29,369
Here's a picture of
you wearing the belt.

482
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:33,171
See there? This is in July.

483
00:28:33,345 --> 00:28:37,874
Before you started going
with Dwayne. See there?

484
00:28:38,817 --> 00:28:41,184
Now, these two

485
00:28:42,120 --> 00:28:46,854
are pictures of Dwayne
wearing the belt buckle

486
00:28:47,025 --> 00:28:50,393
just before you broke
up with him. See there?

487
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:55,296
Yet the police found it in
your possession this morning.

488
00:28:55,467 --> 00:28:57,698
- How could that be?
- I won that belt buckle

489
00:28:57,869 --> 00:28:59,549
because I used to be
the best at something.

490
00:28:59,705 --> 00:29:02,641
I'd have never given it to
somebody like Dwayne ever.

491
00:29:02,808 --> 00:29:05,243
Then why was he wearing
it when he was killed?

492
00:29:07,679 --> 00:29:10,012
You took it off him, didn't you?

493
00:29:10,182 --> 00:29:11,445
After you killed him.

494
00:29:11,617 --> 00:29:15,816
Because, like you say, this belt
buckle means more to you than anything.

495
00:29:15,988 --> 00:29:20,221
And you weren't about to
see him with it for all eternity.

496
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,091
Were you?

497
00:29:25,697 --> 00:29:27,188
Spoke to Bob Brooks.

498
00:29:27,366 --> 00:29:29,494
Cissy Lockwood was
paroled two months ago,

499
00:29:29,668 --> 00:29:34,333
and she's working not five miles
from here at the CanCan Dry Cleaners.

500
00:29:44,983 --> 00:29:46,474
- Thank you.
- Okay.

501
00:29:46,652 --> 00:29:49,053
So you mean Ben Matlock
doesn't really run around naked

502
00:29:49,221 --> 00:29:51,122
every chance he gets?

503
00:29:51,290 --> 00:29:54,226
- No, the photograph was a fake.
- Could have fooled me.

504
00:29:54,393 --> 00:29:57,557
Cissy, where were you the day
before yesterday around 8 a.m.?

505
00:29:58,096 --> 00:29:59,428
Where do you think I was?

506
00:29:59,931 --> 00:30:02,867
Well, I think you were
trespassing in Ben's house,

507
00:30:03,302 --> 00:30:05,102
getting back at him
for putting you in prison.

508
00:30:05,237 --> 00:30:07,468
Well, for your information,
I was in San Antonio

509
00:30:07,639 --> 00:30:10,006
helping my daddy
celebrate his retirement.

510
00:30:10,175 --> 00:30:12,235
Got back yesterday afternoon.

511
00:30:12,411 --> 00:30:15,074
Besides that, I don't hold
anything against Ben Matlock.

512
00:30:15,247 --> 00:30:17,682
He was just doing his job.

513
00:30:17,849 --> 00:30:20,751
Fixed that fuel line for
you, Cissy. Runs like a top.

514
00:30:20,919 --> 00:30:23,946
Thank you, Josh. You are a doll.

515
00:30:26,091 --> 00:30:27,252
Everything okay here?

516
00:30:27,426 --> 00:30:31,090
Oh, yeah. Conrad
and me's old friends.

517
00:30:32,331 --> 00:30:35,165
Stop by next time
you're out this way.

518
00:30:36,401 --> 00:30:38,267
Yeah, I will.

519
00:30:42,140 --> 00:30:43,938
She really was in San Antonio?

520
00:30:44,109 --> 00:30:46,772
- Yeah, she was there.
- And you checked?

521
00:30:46,945 --> 00:30:48,573
Yes.

522
00:30:49,281 --> 00:30:52,513
- You know who else is out on parole?
- Who?

523
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:55,279
That model you used to date.

524
00:30:56,021 --> 00:30:57,819
Carla? MATLOCK: Mm.

525
00:30:59,124 --> 00:31:01,150
Ooh, Carla Royce.

526
00:31:01,326 --> 00:31:03,056
Carla Royce. Carla Royce.

527
00:31:03,228 --> 00:31:07,825
Yeah. Carla Royce was this
woman that I met in New York,

528
00:31:07,999 --> 00:31:11,594
gorgeous, that I was nuts about.

529
00:31:11,903 --> 00:31:15,431
She came to Atlanta for a
shoot, so I went to watch her work.

530
00:31:15,607 --> 00:31:22,878
And this photographer she
was posing for... Harry Samuels?

531
00:31:23,048 --> 00:31:25,847
Yeah... was having
real problems.

532
00:31:28,153 --> 00:31:30,233
Now, get back in there
and do exactly as you're told,

533
00:31:30,389 --> 00:31:32,119
or you're fired. You got that?

534
00:31:32,290 --> 00:31:33,349
What?

535
00:31:33,525 --> 00:31:35,645
I hear you've been bad-mouthing me.
- Jackie.

536
00:31:35,794 --> 00:31:37,729
Spengler's is not
interested in using my people

537
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:40,177
for their Christmas catalog.
I hear you're the reason why.

538
00:31:40,332 --> 00:31:42,172
All I told them is they
could stay under budget

539
00:31:42,334 --> 00:31:44,030
if they used less
expensive models.

540
00:31:45,437 --> 00:31:47,565
You told their art
director that my models

541
00:31:48,940 --> 00:31:51,102
tend to be under-accomplished
and overpriced!

542
00:31:51,276 --> 00:31:52,956
Wait, wait, they
misunderstood me.

543
00:31:53,111 --> 00:31:54,135
Please don't do that!

544
00:31:54,312 --> 00:31:56,781
I don't like it when people
talk behind my back!

545
00:31:56,948 --> 00:32:00,112
If you've got something to
say, then say it to my face!

546
00:32:00,285 --> 00:32:02,811
Jackie, please calm down.

547
00:32:07,192 --> 00:32:10,094
You have crossed
over the line, Harry.

548
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:11,821
This is war.

549
00:32:11,997 --> 00:32:15,263
And believe me,
when the dust clears,

550
00:32:15,434 --> 00:32:17,266
there's only going to
be one of us standing.

551
00:32:17,436 --> 00:32:19,632
And it isn't going to be you.

552
00:32:19,805 --> 00:32:22,566
<i>Jackie Whitman was the biggest
agent in the modeling business,</i>

553
00:32:22,707 --> 00:32:25,302
<i>and she could destroy Harry.</i>

554
00:32:26,378 --> 00:32:28,711
All right, lunch. Be back at 3.

555
00:32:32,217 --> 00:32:34,686
That's some argument old
Harry had with that lady, huh?

556
00:32:34,853 --> 00:32:37,982
That lady is my
agent, Jackie Whitman.

557
00:32:38,156 --> 00:32:41,354
Poor Harry. He really blew it.

558
00:32:41,526 --> 00:32:43,166
She can really keep
him from getting work?

559
00:32:43,295 --> 00:32:44,319
You bet.

560
00:32:44,496 --> 00:32:48,092
That'll be the last major
spread he does for a long time.

561
00:33:17,529 --> 00:33:18,588
Hi, Harry.

562
00:33:19,531 --> 00:33:22,126
I called to see if you wanted
any lunch. Where you been?

563
00:33:22,701 --> 00:33:24,135
Wild-goose chase.

564
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:28,496
What do you mean,
wild-goose chase?

565
00:33:28,974 --> 00:33:31,239
Just what I said.

566
00:33:38,984 --> 00:33:41,977
Harry, you been here long?

567
00:33:42,387 --> 00:33:44,049
I just got in. Why?

568
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:47,557
I got good news and bad news.

569
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:58,394
The good news is Jackie Whitman's
not gonna bother you anymore.

570
00:33:58,970 --> 00:34:00,905
Well, what's up?

571
00:34:01,072 --> 00:34:03,769
Carla's agent, Jackie Whitman
was murdered this afternoon.

572
00:34:06,177 --> 00:34:08,646
I heard that on the news.

573
00:34:08,813 --> 00:34:11,009
Your agent. I'm sorry.

574
00:34:11,917 --> 00:34:15,012
They arrested my
friend, Harry Samuels.

575
00:34:15,186 --> 00:34:17,746
- Oh.
- I've known Harry for years.

576
00:34:17,923 --> 00:34:19,721
He's impulsive and
he's temperamental,

577
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:21,416
but he's not a murderer.

578
00:34:22,427 --> 00:34:23,690
Oh.

579
00:34:23,862 --> 00:34:26,730
His answering service got a
message from somebody named Jackie

580
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:30,391
asking him to meet her at
the park so they could talk.

581
00:34:30,569 --> 00:34:32,834
He went to the park
and no one was there.

582
00:34:33,004 --> 00:34:35,496
And when he got back to
the studio, he found her dead.

583
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:39,108
Think somebody set him up?
- Yeah.

584
00:34:40,745 --> 00:34:42,111
He can pay your fee, Ben.

585
00:34:43,748 --> 00:34:46,411
<i>The next day, Ben found
out something about Carla</i>

586
00:34:46,585 --> 00:34:47,678
<i>that flipped me out.</i>

587
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,452
Oh, yeah, here, take a look.

588
00:34:49,621 --> 00:34:52,614
Oh, here, use this.

589
00:34:54,526 --> 00:34:56,085
Ooh.

590
00:34:56,261 --> 00:34:58,821
Boy, that Lauren is
a beauty, isn't she?

591
00:34:58,997 --> 00:35:01,762
- So's Carla.
- Oh, yeah.

592
00:35:01,933 --> 00:35:07,065
Look at Carla's smile and
poise. She's a born model.

593
00:35:07,238 --> 00:35:10,072
I know. So was her sister.

594
00:35:11,376 --> 00:35:12,969
- Sister?
- Mm-hm.

595
00:35:13,144 --> 00:35:17,138
Her name was Monica. Whew,
we're talking major good looks.

596
00:35:17,315 --> 00:35:19,807
Once she and Carla started
working, they never stopped.

597
00:35:19,985 --> 00:35:21,851
Only Monica couldn't
handle the life.

598
00:35:23,555 --> 00:35:24,853
Drugs?

599
00:35:25,023 --> 00:35:27,822
Oh, yeah, in a big way. Whew.

600
00:35:27,993 --> 00:35:29,359
She dropped out
about a year ago,

601
00:35:29,527 --> 00:35:31,167
and the next thing we
heard, she was dead.

602
00:35:31,296 --> 00:35:33,094
It was a, um, car
accident or something.

603
00:35:33,264 --> 00:35:36,496
And then Carla stopped working
for a month or two after that.

604
00:35:36,668 --> 00:35:41,470
When she came back, she was
really determined, almost driven.

605
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:43,131
She hasn't stopped since.

606
00:35:43,308 --> 00:35:46,142
Monica. Who was her agent?

607
00:35:46,311 --> 00:35:48,780
Same as Carla's. Jackie Whitman.

608
00:35:48,947 --> 00:35:54,614
How long have you been a
fashion model, Miss Royce?

609
00:35:55,153 --> 00:35:56,644
About four years.

610
00:35:56,821 --> 00:36:01,691
Your sister, Monica, started modeling
about that same time, didn't she?

611
00:36:02,327 --> 00:36:05,126
- That's right. MATLOCK:
What happened to her?

612
00:36:05,830 --> 00:36:08,493
She died in a car
accident almost a year ago.

613
00:36:08,667 --> 00:36:10,101
Hmm.

614
00:36:10,268 --> 00:36:11,668
Who was her agent?

615
00:36:12,270 --> 00:36:13,363
Jackie Whitman.

616
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:18,374
Your sister, Monica, was arrested once
for possession of cocaine, wasn't she?

617
00:36:18,543 --> 00:36:22,173
- What's my sister got to do with this?
- Please answer the question.

618
00:36:22,681 --> 00:36:24,377
Yes, she was arrested.

619
00:36:24,549 --> 00:36:26,814
- Was she prosecuted?
- No.

620
00:36:26,985 --> 00:36:28,385
How come?

621
00:36:28,586 --> 00:36:29,918
The charges were dropped.

622
00:36:30,622 --> 00:36:32,853
The charges were dropped?

623
00:36:33,124 --> 00:36:36,117
That would be very
difficult to get done.

624
00:36:36,428 --> 00:36:38,363
Who got the charges dropped?

625
00:36:39,564 --> 00:36:41,624
Jackie Whitman. MATLOCK: Oh.

626
00:36:42,567 --> 00:36:46,698
So Jackie Whitman knew
your sister had a drug problem.

627
00:36:47,872 --> 00:36:49,170
Yes.

628
00:36:49,340 --> 00:36:52,936
Did she ever suggest that
Monica go for treatment?

629
00:36:53,778 --> 00:36:54,802
No.

630
00:36:54,979 --> 00:36:57,346
Did you ever suggest
that she get treatment?

631
00:36:57,515 --> 00:37:00,485
I begged her. I pleaded.
I even threatened her. I...

632
00:37:00,652 --> 00:37:03,012
She had more control
over your sister than you did,

633
00:37:03,154 --> 00:37:04,452
and you hated her for it.

634
00:37:04,989 --> 00:37:06,958
When Jackie walked
into that darkroom,

635
00:37:07,125 --> 00:37:09,424
you stabbed her to death
with those scissors, didn't you?

636
00:37:09,594 --> 00:37:10,892
Absolutely not!

637
00:37:11,062 --> 00:37:16,023
The proof is in the acid burn
that's on your lower left arm.

638
00:37:17,836 --> 00:37:19,356
I don't know what
you're talking about.

639
00:37:19,504 --> 00:37:23,635
I'm talking about the burn you sustained
when you stabbed Jackie Whitman.

640
00:37:23,808 --> 00:37:27,370
She fell against the counter,
knocked over a bottle of acid,

641
00:37:27,545 --> 00:37:29,385
and part of it splashed
on your arm, didn't it?

642
00:37:29,547 --> 00:37:32,312
- No.
- That's why

643
00:37:32,484 --> 00:37:35,943
during the rest of the shoot,

644
00:37:36,654 --> 00:37:41,683
you took great pains to hide
your left arm from the camera.

645
00:37:43,695 --> 00:37:47,029
I have a burn on my arm, yes.

646
00:37:47,198 --> 00:37:51,431
But it's from spilling
hot coffee on it, not acid.

647
00:37:52,070 --> 00:37:56,735
That's an acid burn.
You know it, and I know it,

648
00:37:57,709 --> 00:38:02,670
and this police
report proves it.

649
00:38:05,116 --> 00:38:09,247
A lot of bottles of makeup
got broken that afternoon

650
00:38:09,420 --> 00:38:12,720
during the argument between
Harry and Jackie, didn't they?

651
00:38:12,891 --> 00:38:14,325
The place was a mess.

652
00:38:14,492 --> 00:38:17,758
Harry's assistant, Frannie
Morrissey, cleaned it up.

653
00:38:17,929 --> 00:38:24,096
Also, she replaced all of the
old makeup bottles with new ones.

654
00:38:24,402 --> 00:38:26,268
Now, that means

655
00:38:27,005 --> 00:38:30,965
the only fingerprints that
should be on those bottles

656
00:38:31,142 --> 00:38:34,078
when the police
dusted after the murder

657
00:38:34,579 --> 00:38:36,013
were hers.

658
00:38:36,181 --> 00:38:39,549
Would you please
look at this police report

659
00:38:39,717 --> 00:38:42,778
and read the names of the
people whose prints were found

660
00:38:42,954 --> 00:38:45,822
on one of those bottles?

661
00:38:48,126 --> 00:38:50,595
"Frances Morrissey and..."

662
00:38:53,898 --> 00:38:55,890
"Carla Royce."

663
00:38:56,301 --> 00:38:57,599
That's you.

664
00:38:57,769 --> 00:39:04,107
How did your fingerprints get all
over one of those brand-new bottles?

665
00:39:11,115 --> 00:39:13,380
I'll check on Carla.

666
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:16,416
Holy. Look at the time.

667
00:39:16,588 --> 00:39:18,454
Oh, Lord.

668
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:24,254
I guess he took all the
money out of the drawer

669
00:39:24,429 --> 00:39:26,421
and then he told us
to get down on the floor

670
00:39:26,598 --> 00:39:28,533
and stay there till he was gone.

671
00:39:28,700 --> 00:39:31,795
But when I heard him start up
his car, I looked up as he drove off

672
00:39:31,970 --> 00:39:36,237
and I saw his license
plate, CUY4J7.

673
00:39:36,407 --> 00:39:38,137
The same plate which,
as was stipulated,

674
00:39:38,309 --> 00:39:41,040
was issued last
July to the defendant.

675
00:39:41,212 --> 00:39:42,908
Nothing further, Your Honor.

676
00:39:43,081 --> 00:39:45,141
Mr. Burton.

677
00:39:45,316 --> 00:39:48,616
We all couldn't help but notice that
you arrived a little late, Mr. Matlock.

678
00:39:49,254 --> 00:39:50,984
Everything all right?

679
00:39:51,155 --> 00:39:53,818
- Everything's fine.
- You sure?

680
00:39:53,992 --> 00:39:57,224
I hear you had a little problem with
the planning commission the other day.

681
00:39:57,395 --> 00:39:58,875
You brought the
wrong papers with you?

682
00:39:59,030 --> 00:40:01,158
Objection. Irrelevant.

683
00:40:01,332 --> 00:40:02,823
Goes to credibility, Your Honor.

684
00:40:03,468 --> 00:40:04,595
I'll allow it.

685
00:40:05,470 --> 00:40:07,630
Rumor has it that you recently
showed up at Chez Munroe

686
00:40:07,772 --> 00:40:10,332
for a party that didn't
exist. That right?

687
00:40:10,508 --> 00:40:12,108
Yeah, but the reason for that...

688
00:40:12,210 --> 00:40:13,576
Is this you, Mr. Matlock?

689
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:16,711
No.

690
00:40:16,881 --> 00:40:19,043
Well, who is it? Your evil twin?

691
00:40:19,217 --> 00:40:20,241
No.

692
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:24,253
That's my head, but not
my hind end. Ask anybody.

693
00:40:25,189 --> 00:40:28,682
- Anybody?
- Well, no, not anybody.

694
00:40:28,860 --> 00:40:31,489
- That's not my hind end.
- Mr. Matlock. Language.

695
00:40:31,663 --> 00:40:32,926
- Rear end.
- Language.

696
00:40:33,097 --> 00:40:34,793
Tush. Give me a break.

697
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:36,696
Your Honor.

698
00:40:38,903 --> 00:40:40,929
You may proceed, Mr. Burton.

699
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:44,234
Mr. Matlock, do you really expect
these good people to believe

700
00:40:44,409 --> 00:40:46,901
that somebody as flamboyant
as you obviously are

701
00:40:47,078 --> 00:40:51,482
can say for certain it was my client,
whose face you admit you never saw,

702
00:40:51,649 --> 00:40:54,209
was without a doubt the person
who robbed that convenience store?

703
00:40:54,352 --> 00:40:58,790
I picked him out of a lineup. I
heard his voice. I saw his shoes.

704
00:40:58,957 --> 00:41:02,257
- You saw his shoes?
- Yeah.

705
00:41:02,427 --> 00:41:04,293
What did his shoes look like?

706
00:41:04,462 --> 00:41:08,399
They were running shoes,
black, with purple and pink trim.

707
00:41:08,566 --> 00:41:09,693
What brand were they?

708
00:41:11,102 --> 00:41:12,593
- I don't know.
- Well, then.

709
00:41:15,473 --> 00:41:18,739
Perhaps this will
refresh your memory.

710
00:41:24,649 --> 00:41:27,448
So which shoe was it?

711
00:41:27,618 --> 00:41:29,416
This one?

712
00:41:29,587 --> 00:41:31,886
Or maybe it was this one.

713
00:41:32,757 --> 00:41:34,248
I can't say.

714
00:41:35,193 --> 00:41:37,822
- Can't you even try?
- I'd be guessing.

715
00:41:37,996 --> 00:41:39,988
- You'd be guessing?
- I'd be guessing.

716
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:42,656
Just like you did when you
picked my client out of that lineup.

717
00:41:42,834 --> 00:41:44,154
- Right, Mr. Matlock?
- No.

718
00:41:44,302 --> 00:41:45,497
Nothing further.

719
00:41:58,116 --> 00:41:59,584
- Gonna be at home?
- No.

720
00:41:59,751 --> 00:42:01,982
I'm gonna stay and see
what the jury has to say.

721
00:42:02,153 --> 00:42:04,748
What if they find
that guy not guilty?

722
00:42:04,922 --> 00:42:08,017
I don't know. Then... Then
they find him not guilty.

723
00:42:08,192 --> 00:42:11,128
I'll look like a jackass. Hmm.

724
00:42:14,165 --> 00:42:16,691
Has the jury reached a verdict?

725
00:42:17,301 --> 00:42:18,461
We have, Your Honor.

726
00:42:18,803 --> 00:42:21,432
We find the defendant
guilty as charged.

727
00:42:22,840 --> 00:42:25,207
The defendant will
return to this courtroom

728
00:42:25,376 --> 00:42:27,971
at 9:00 on the 23rd of
this month for sentencing.

729
00:42:28,513 --> 00:42:29,537
Court is adjourned.

730
00:42:33,818 --> 00:42:36,049
They believed you after all.

731
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:38,655
Congratulations, Ben, you
pulled another one out of the fire.

732
00:42:52,537 --> 00:42:54,506
Carla's in France?

733
00:42:54,672 --> 00:42:56,607
Maybe it is Dave Burton.

734
00:42:56,774 --> 00:43:01,872
Well, I haven't gotten
any phone calls for a while.

735
00:43:02,380 --> 00:43:05,441
So let's forget it and
have a nice bowl of chili.

736
00:43:05,616 --> 00:43:08,518
Oh, no, no, no.
I don't think so.

737
00:43:08,686 --> 00:43:11,679
Um, no, I have a lunch
meeting tomorrow,

738
00:43:11,856 --> 00:43:14,849
and those onions you
use are really lethal.

739
00:43:15,026 --> 00:43:16,221
Good night.

740
00:43:16,694 --> 00:43:18,595
What about you, Conrad?

741
00:43:18,763 --> 00:43:23,292
I'd better not. I got a
date in two days. No.

742
00:44:28,966 --> 00:44:31,401
I really hated prison.

743
00:44:31,569 --> 00:44:34,596
- Oh. Cissy.
- Only thing that kept me going

744
00:44:34,772 --> 00:44:37,674
was thinking about all the things I
was gonna do to you once I got out.

745
00:44:38,075 --> 00:44:39,941
Thought you were in San Antonio.

746
00:44:40,111 --> 00:44:43,104
My boyfriend, Josh,
he's real handy with locks.

747
00:44:43,281 --> 00:44:46,877
Oh, you're the one that's
been messing with my papers

748
00:44:47,051 --> 00:44:49,714
and sending me
to the wrong parties

749
00:44:49,887 --> 00:44:53,654
and publishing that phony
picture of my hind end.

750
00:44:53,824 --> 00:44:55,156
And now you're gonna kill me?

751
00:44:55,326 --> 00:44:57,124
Bingo.

752
00:44:57,695 --> 00:44:59,596
I really hadn't
planned to kill you,

753
00:45:00,364 --> 00:45:02,390
I just wanted to
make you suffer.

754
00:45:03,034 --> 00:45:07,768
Wreck your life bit
by bit, day by day.

755
00:45:08,139 --> 00:45:10,108
But when I watched
that trial today

756
00:45:10,274 --> 00:45:12,354
and saw how you got everybody
around here brainwashed

757
00:45:12,510 --> 00:45:15,605
into thinking you're God's gift
to truth and justice, I got mad.

758
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:17,976
I said to myself,
"To hell with it.

759
00:45:18,149 --> 00:45:20,029
Give him what he deserves
and get it over with."

760
00:45:20,151 --> 00:45:21,414
No, no, no.

761
00:45:21,586 --> 00:45:24,186
Cissy, you don't... You don't...
You don't have to kill me, Cissy.

762
00:45:24,288 --> 00:45:25,756
I mean, you're out.

763
00:45:25,923 --> 00:45:29,052
You're out of prison now, and
you got this nice new boyfriend,

764
00:45:29,227 --> 00:45:32,095
and you could keep
playing nasty tricks on me.

765
00:45:32,263 --> 00:45:33,492
No!

766
00:45:33,664 --> 00:45:35,724
Well, wait a minute.

767
00:45:36,234 --> 00:45:38,794
- What are you doing?
- I'm praying.

768
00:45:38,970 --> 00:45:41,906
If I'm gonna go see Jesus, I
want him to know I'm coming.

769
00:45:45,576 --> 00:45:47,010
I thought I heard you.

770
00:45:47,178 --> 00:45:50,012
Yeah. Recognized
your motorcycle.

771
00:45:50,181 --> 00:45:52,980
Took me a minute, but I finally
figured out where I'd seen it before.

772
00:45:53,150 --> 00:45:55,619
Next time, try parking three
blocks to the south, Cissy.

773
00:45:55,786 --> 00:45:57,846
- Thanks.
- It's okay.

774
00:45:58,022 --> 00:45:59,046
Wanna call the police?

775
00:46:04,128 --> 00:46:06,495
What's happening? I
saw Conrad make a U-turn.

776
00:46:06,664 --> 00:46:09,566
Uh-huh. Hello, Cliff.
This is Cissy Lockwood.

777
00:46:09,734 --> 00:46:11,430
I sent her to prison
a few years ago,

778
00:46:11,602 --> 00:46:14,037
and she stopped by
to say everything's fine

779
00:46:14,205 --> 00:46:16,640
and there's no hard feelings.

780
00:46:16,807 --> 00:46:18,742
And to have a
nice bowl of chili.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
